IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 14 to 18A: repeal, expiry, continuance and re-enactment.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- s 14(2) and s 16(4) (the last moment of a day on which an enactment expires) are in tas-interpretation-time.l4, with the rest of the Act's counting of time.

§ `s 14: repeal of a repealing Act`

-- src:287 | (1) Where an Act, passed after 5th August 1853, repeals an enactment by which any former enactment was repealed, it shall not have the effect of reviving such former enactment unless express words for that purpose are included in such repealing Act.
@ref s 14(1) consequence (src:287)
GIVEN `the day the repealing Act was passed` IS A DATE
      `express words for that purpose are included in the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1): the repealing Act does not have the effect of reviving the former enactment` `the day the repealing Act was passed` `express words for that purpose are included in the repealing Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`s 14(1): a repealing Act was passed after 5th August 1853` `the day the repealing Act was passed`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `express words for that purpose are included in the repealing Act` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 14(1): the repealing Act does not have the effect of reviving the former enactment` (Date 6 8 1853) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1): the repealing Act does not have the effect of reviving the former enactment` (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1): the repealing Act does not have the effect of reviving the former enactment` (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(1): the repealing Act does not have the effect of reviving the former enactment` (Date 5 8 1853) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(1): the repealing Act does not have the effect of reviving the former enactment` (Date 4 8 1853) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 15: continuance of provisions pending operation of those substituted, and of existing regulations`

-- src:293 | (1) Where an Act repeals, wholly or in part, a former Act and substitutes provisions in lieu thereof, the repealed provisions shall remain in force until the substituted provisions come into operation.
@ref s 15(1) (src:293)
GIVEN `the Act repeals, wholly or in part, a former Act and substitutes provisions in lieu thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the substituted provisions come into operation` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(1): the repealed provisions remain in force on the day` `the Act repeals, wholly or in part, a former Act and substitutes provisions in lieu thereof` `the day the substituted provisions come into operation` `the day in question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the Act repeals, wholly or in part, a former Act and substitutes provisions in lieu thereof`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the day in question` BELOW `the day the substituted provisions come into operation` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- "until": the day the substituted provisions come into operation is outside the period

-- src:295 | (2) Where the repealing Act contains power to make any regulations, all regulations made under the repealed Act, so far as the same are not inconsistent with the repealing Act, shall remain in force until rescinded under the repealing Act, and shall be deemed to have been made for the purposes of the repealing Act and may be altered, amended, or rescinded under that Act.
@ref s 15(2) (src:295)
GIVEN `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2): the regulation made under the repealed Act is within the saving` `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the repealing Act contains power to make regulations`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the regulation was made under the repealed Act`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           IF `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation has been rescinded under the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2): the regulation remains in force` `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act` `the regulation has been rescinded under the repealing Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 15(2): the regulation made under the repealed Act is within the saving` `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN IF `the regulation has been rescinded under the repealing Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE   -- "until rescinded"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(2): the regulation is deemed made for the purposes of the repealing Act, and may be altered, amended or rescinded under it` `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act` MEANS
    `s 15(2): the regulation made under the repealed Act is within the saving` `the repealing Act contains power to make regulations` `the regulation was made under the repealed Act` `the regulation is inconsistent with the repealing Act`

-- src:297 | (3) Where regulations made under a repealed Act have remained in force after the repeal of such Act, any general regulations made under any Act which has been substituted for the repealed Act shall supersede and have the effect of rescinding those made under the repealed Act, unless the contrary is expressly provided.
@ref s 15(3) (src:297)
GIVEN `the regulations made under the repealed Act have remained in force after its repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new regulations are general regulations made under an Act substituted for the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15(3): the new general regulations supersede and rescind the regulations made under the repealed Act` `the regulations made under the repealed Act have remained in force after its repeal` `the new regulations are general regulations made under an Act substituted for the repealed Act` `the contrary is expressly provided` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the regulations made under the repealed Act have remained in force after its repeal`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the new regulations are general regulations made under an Act substituted for the repealed Act`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 15(1): the repealed provisions remain in force on the day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(1): the repealed provisions remain in force on the day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(1): the repealed provisions remain in force on the day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(1): the repealed provisions remain in force on the day` FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation made under the repealed Act is within the saving` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation made under the repealed Act is within the saving` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation made under the repealed Act is within the saving` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation made under the repealed Act is within the saving` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation remains in force` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation remains in force` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation remains in force` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation remains in force` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation is deemed made for the purposes of the repealing Act, and may be altered, amended or rescinded under it` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the regulation is deemed made for the purposes of the repealing Act, and may be altered, amended or rescinded under it` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(3): the new general regulations supersede and rescind the regulations made under the repealed Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(3): the new general regulations supersede and rescind the regulations made under the repealed Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(3): the new general regulations supersede and rescind the regulations made under the repealed Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(3): the new general regulations supersede and rescind the regulations made under the repealed Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 16: effect of repeal, expiry and the like`

DECLARE `Matter the repeal or expiry does not affect` IS ONE OF
    `anything not in force or existing at the time the repeal or expiry took or takes effect`
    `the previous operation of the enactment, or anything duly done or suffered under it`
    `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment`
    `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment`
    `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment`

-- src:301 | (1) Where an Act repeals any other enactment then, unless the contrary is expressly provided, such repeal shall not –
-- src:303 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing at the time such repeal took, or shall take, effect;
-- src:305 | (b) affect the previous operation of any enactment so repealed or anything duly done or suffered under any enactment so repealed;
-- src:307 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation, or liability acquired, accrued, or incurred under any enactment so repealed;
-- src:309 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture, or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against any enactment so repealed; or
-- src:311 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture, or punishment as aforesaid –
-- src:313 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy may be instituted, continued, or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture, or punishment may be imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed.
@ref s 16(1) (src:301-313)
GIVEN `an Act repeals the enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter the repeal or expiry does not affect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1): the repeal does not revive or affect the matter` `an Act repeals the enactment` `the contrary is expressly provided` matter MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an Act repeals the enactment`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:315 | (2) Where an enactment expires or has expired, then, unless the contrary is expressly provided, the expiry shall not –
-- src:317 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing at the time the expiry took, or takes, effect;
-- src:319 | (b) affect the previous operation of any enactment so expired or anything duly done or suffered under any enactment so expired;
-- src:321 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation, or liability acquired, accrued, or incurred under any enactment so expired;
-- src:323 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture, or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against any enactment so expired; or
-- src:325 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture, or punishment –
-- src:327 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy may be instituted, continued, or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture, or punishment may be imposed as if the enactment had not expired.
@ref s 16(2) (src:315-327)
GIVEN `the enactment expires or has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter the repeal or expiry does not affect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2): the expiry does not revive or affect the matter` `the enactment expires or has expired` `the contrary is expressly provided` matter MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the enactment expires or has expired`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The closing words of s 16(1) and of s 16(2) say what may then be done, and they name only two of the five matters:
-- the investigation, legal proceeding or remedy (paragraph (e)), and the penalty, forfeiture or punishment (paragraph (d)).
-- src:309 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture, or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against any enactment so repealed; or
-- src:311 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture, or punishment as aforesaid –
-- src:313 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy may be instituted, continued, or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture, or punishment may be imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed.
-- src:323 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture, or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against any enactment so expired; or
-- src:325 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture, or punishment –
-- src:327 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding, or remedy may be instituted, continued, or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture, or punishment may be imposed as if the enactment had not expired.
@ref s 16(1) closing words and s 16(2) closing words (src:309-313) (src:323-327)
GIVEN `the repeal or expiry is one to which section 16(1) or (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter the repeal or expiry does not affect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) and (2) closing words: the investigation, proceeding, remedy or penalty may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed or the enactment had not expired` `the repeal or expiry is one to which section 16(1) or (2) applies` `the contrary is expressly provided` matter MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the repeal or expiry is one to which section 16(1) or (2) applies`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (matter EQUALS `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` OR matter EQUALS `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Way a regulation comes to an end` IS ONE OF
    `the regulation is rescinded`
    `the regulation expires`
    `the regulation ceases to have effect owing to the repeal of the enactment under which it is made`
    `the regulation ceases to have effect owing to the expiry of the enactment under which it is made`

DECLARE `Way an enactment or regulation stops` IS ONE OF
    `as repealed`
    `as expired`

-- src:329 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) apply to and in relation to any regulations that –
-- src:331 | (a) are rescinded or expire; or
-- src:333 | (b) cease to have effect owing to the repeal or expiry of the enactment under which the regulations are made –
-- src:335 | in the same way as those subsections apply to and in relation to enactments that are or have been repealed or, as the case may be, that expire or have expired.
@ref s 16(3) (src:329-335)
GIVEN ending IS A `Way a regulation comes to an end`
GIVETH A `Way an enactment or regulation stops`
`s 16(3): subsections (1) and (2) apply to the regulation that ends in the way` ending MEANS
    CONSIDER ending
    WHEN `the regulation is rescinded` THEN `as repealed`
    WHEN `the regulation expires` THEN `as expired`
    WHEN `the regulation ceases to have effect owing to the repeal of the enactment under which it is made` THEN `as repealed`
    WHEN `the regulation ceases to have effect owing to the expiry of the enactment under which it is made` THEN `as expired`

GIVEN ending IS A `Way a regulation comes to an end`
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter the repeal or expiry does not affect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16: the ending of the regulation does not revive or affect the matter` ending `the contrary is expressly provided` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 16(3): subsections (1) and (2) apply to the regulation that ends in the way` ending
    WHEN `as repealed` THEN `s 16(1): the repeal does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE `the contrary is expressly provided` matter
    WHEN `as expired` THEN `s 16(2): the expiry does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE `the contrary is expressly provided` matter

#ASSERT `s 16(1): the repeal does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE FALSE `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(1): the repeal does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE FALSE `anything not in force or existing at the time the repeal or expiry took or takes effect` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(1): the repeal does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE FALSE `the previous operation of the enactment, or anything duly done or suffered under it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(1): the repeal does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE TRUE `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1): the repeal does not revive or affect the matter` FALSE FALSE `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the expiry does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE FALSE `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the expiry does not revive or affect the matter` TRUE TRUE `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(2): the expiry does not revive or affect the matter` FALSE FALSE `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
