#ASSERT `s 16(1) and (2) closing words: the investigation, proceeding, remedy or penalty may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed or the enactment had not expired` TRUE FALSE `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) and (2) closing words: the investigation, proceeding, remedy or penalty may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed or the enactment had not expired` TRUE FALSE `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the enactment` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 16(1) and (2) closing words: the investigation, proceeding, remedy or penalty may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed or the enactment had not expired` TRUE TRUE `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(1) and (2) closing words: the investigation, proceeding, remedy or penalty may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been passed or the enactment had not expired` FALSE FALSE `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against the enactment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16(3): subsections (1) and (2) apply to the regulation that ends in the way` `the regulation is rescinded` EQUALS `as repealed`
#ASSERT `s 16(3): subsections (1) and (2) apply to the regulation that ends in the way` `the regulation expires` EQUALS `as expired`
#ASSERT `s 16(3): subsections (1) and (2) apply to the regulation that ends in the way` `the regulation ceases to have effect owing to the repeal of the enactment under which it is made` EQUALS `as repealed`
#ASSERT `s 16(3): subsections (1) and (2) apply to the regulation that ends in the way` `the regulation ceases to have effect owing to the expiry of the enactment under which it is made` EQUALS `as expired`
