§ `s 17: references to repealed provisions`

DECLARE `Re-enactment` HAS
    `the provision repealed` IS A STRING
    `the provision re-enacted` IS A STRING

-- src:339 | 17. References to repealed provisions
-- src:341 | Where an Act repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, any provisions of a former Act, references in any other Act to the provisions so repealed shall be construed as references to the provisions so re-enacted.
@ref s 17 (src:339-341)
GIVEN `the Act repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, provisions of a former Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in another Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17: a reference to the provisions repealed is to be construed as a reference to the provisions re-enacted` `the Act repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, provisions of a former Act` `the reference is in another Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the Act repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, provisions of a former Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the reference is in another Act`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN reenactments IS A LIST OF `Re-enactment`
      reference IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 17: the provision that the reference to the provision is to be construed as a reference to` reenactments reference MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the provision repealed` EQUALS reference) reenactments
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (r's `the provision re-enacted`)

#ASSERT `s 17: a reference to the provisions repealed is to be construed as a reference to the provisions re-enacted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17: a reference to the provisions repealed is to be construed as a reference to the provisions re-enacted` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17: a reference to the provisions repealed is to be construed as a reference to the provisions re-enacted` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 17: the provision that the reference to the provision is to be construed as a reference to` (LIST `Re-enactment` WITH `the provision repealed` IS "section 4 of the old Act", `the provision re-enacted` IS "section 9 of the new Act") "section 4 of the old Act" EQUALS JUST "section 9 of the new Act"
#ASSERT `s 17: the provision that the reference to the provision is to be construed as a reference to` (LIST `Re-enactment` WITH `the provision repealed` IS "section 4 of the old Act", `the provision re-enacted` IS "section 9 of the new Act") "section 5 of the old Act" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17: the provision that the reference to the provision is to be construed as a reference to` (EMPTY) "section 4 of the old Act" EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 18: effect of repeal by consolidating Acts`

DECLARE `Matter dealt with by the corresponding provisions` IS ONE OF
    `the constitution or setting up of districts, areas or local divisions`
    `the constitution or setting up of councils, corporations, boards, trusts or other executive bodies`
    `the constitution or setting up of an office`
    `the appointment of officers, or the appointment or election of members of a body so constituted`
    `the making or issuing of proclamations, orders, warrants, certificates or other documents of authority`
    `any other matter`

GIVEN `the Act repeals and consolidates, with or without amendment, enactments relating to a subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act enacts provisions substantially corresponding to those repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `Matter dealt with by the corresponding provisions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18: the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` `the Act repeals and consolidates, with or without amendment, enactments relating to a subject` `the Act enacts provisions substantially corresponding to those repealed` matter MEANS
    `the Act repeals and consolidates, with or without amendment, enactments relating to a subject` AND `the Act enacts provisions substantially corresponding to those repealed` AND NOT (matter EQUALS `any other matter`)

-- src:343 | 18. Effect of repeal by consolidating Acts
-- src:345 | Where an Act repeals and consolidates, with or without amendment, enactments relating to any subject and enacts provisions substantially corresponding to those so repealed, for –
-- src:347 | (a) the constitution or setting up of –
-- src:349 | (i) any districts, areas, or local divisions;
-- src:351 | (ii) councils, corporations, boards, trusts, or other executive bodies; or
-- src:353 | (iii) any office;
-- src:355 | (b) the appointment of officers or the appointment or election of members of any body constituted as aforesaid; or
-- src:357 | (c) the making or issuing of proclamations, orders, warrants, certificates, or other documents of authority –
-- src:359 | everything done under such repealed provisions, and existing or in force at the time of such repeal, shall continue in force, so far as is not inconsistent with the repealing Act, and all such districts, areas, divisions, bodies, offices, officers, and documents in existence, in office, or in force shall be deemed to have been constituted, elected, appointed, made, or issued respectively under and for the purposes of the repealing Act.
@ref s 18 (src:343-359)
GIVEN `the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing was done under the repealed provisions and exists or is in force at the time of the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is inconsistent with the repealing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18: the thing continues in force` `the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` `the thing was done under the repealed provisions and exists or is in force at the time of the repeal` `the thing is inconsistent with the repealing Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the repeal is one to which section 18 applies`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the thing was done under the repealed provisions and exists or is in force at the time of the repeal`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           IF `the thing is inconsistent with the repealing Act` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the district, area, division, body, office, officer or document is in existence, in office or in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18: the district, area, division, body, office, officer or document is deemed to have been constituted, elected, appointed, made or issued under and for the purposes of the repealing Act` `the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` `the district, area, division, body, office, officer or document is in existence, in office or in force` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the repeal is one to which section 18 applies`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the district, area, division, body, office, officer or document is in existence, in office or in force`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 18: the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` TRUE TRUE `the constitution or setting up of an office`
#ASSERT `s 18: the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` TRUE TRUE `the making or issuing of proclamations, orders, warrants, certificates or other documents of authority`
#ASSERT `s 18: the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` TRUE TRUE `the appointment of officers, or the appointment or election of members of a body so constituted`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18: the repeal is one to which section 18 applies` TRUE TRUE `any other matter`)
