§ `s 18A: continuing Act to operate from expiration of continued Act`

-- src:361 | 18A. Continuing Act to operate from expiration of continued Act
-- src:363 | When a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament, and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed, that Bill, upon receiving the Governor's assent for and on behalf of the Sovereign (or, if reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure, upon the Sovereign's assents thereto being proclaimed by the Governor) shall, unless the contrary intention appears therein, be deemed to have taken effect in continuing the temporary enactment on and from the date of the expiration thereof; but no person is liable, or shall be subjected, to any punishment, penalty, or forfeiture for or in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by him, contrary to any provision of the temporary enactment, between the date of its expiration and the date of that assent.
@ref s 18A deeming (src:361-363)
GIVEN `a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears in the Bill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 18A: the date from which the Bill is deemed to have taken effect in continuing the temporary enactment` `a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor` `the contrary intention appears in the Bill` `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` MEANS
    IF `a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` AND `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor` AND NOT (`the contrary intention appears in the Bill`)
    THEN JUST `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment`
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears in the Bill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A: the temporary enactment is treated as continued in operation on the day` `a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor` `the contrary intention appears in the Bill` `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` `the day in question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` AND `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "When" and "upon"
           IF `the contrary intention appears in the Bill` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day in question` AT LEAST `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- "on and from": a day before the date of the expiration is outside the period

-- "between the date of its expiration and the date of that assent": both dates are counted in (a fork, see NOTES.md).
-- src:361 | 18A. Continuing Act to operate from expiration of continued Act
-- src:363 | When a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament, and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed, that Bill, upon receiving the Governor's assent for and on behalf of the Sovereign (or, if reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure, upon the Sovereign's assents thereto being proclaimed by the Governor) shall, unless the contrary intention appears therein, be deemed to have taken effect in continuing the temporary enactment on and from the date of the expiration thereof; but no person is liable, or shall be subjected, to any punishment, penalty, or forfeiture for or in respect of anything done or omitted to be done by him, contrary to any provision of the temporary enactment, between the date of its expiration and the date of that assent.
@ref s 18A no liability (src:361-363)
GIVEN `a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` IS A DATE
      `the date of that assent` IS A DATE
      `the day the thing was done or omitted` IS A DATE
      `the thing done or omitted was contrary to a provision of the temporary enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A: the person is not liable to punishment, penalty or forfeiture for the thing done or omitted` `a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor` `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` `the date of that assent` `the day the thing was done or omitted` `the thing done or omitted was contrary to a provision of the temporary enactment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a Bill for continuing a temporary enactment has been introduced into Parliament and, at the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment, has not been passed` AND `the Bill has received the Governor's assent or, if reserved, the Sovereign's assent has been proclaimed by the Governor`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "When" and "upon"
           IF `the day the thing was done or omitted` BELOW `the date of the expiration of the temporary enactment` OR `the day the thing was done or omitted` GREATER THAN `the date of that assent` THEN JUST FALSE   -- "between": outside the period the text fixes
           IF NOT (`the thing done or omitted was contrary to a provision of the temporary enactment`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

